  "residual": "Constructed unique first-moment invariant laws for Markov kernels on complete separable Borel metric spaces preserving first moments and satisfying the original global all-probability-law IsW1Contraction with 0 <= rho < 1. A row-drift criterion derives moment preservation; actual kernel iterates obey geometric coupling-W1 bounds and converge in the constructed transport metric. Both original ContractivePerturbation invariant laws are constructed independently under their two contraction/moment hypotheses. Non-first-moment invariant laws and general occupation-property factorization/ergodic bridges are separate scope."
